{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "pbip-audit",
          "version": "0.2.0",
          "semanticVersion": "0.2.0",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/alexguardiola/pbip-audit-skill",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "A11Y-01",
              "name": "VisualsWithoutAltText",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Visuals without alt text"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Screen readers announce only the visual type when alt text is missing."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "How to verify: Visible, non-decorative, non-slicer visuals with no `general.altText` (counted per page).\nFix: Add alt text that states the insight, or bind it to a measure for dynamic text.",
                "markdown": "**How to verify:** Visible, non-decorative, non-slicer visuals with no `general.altText` (counted per page).\n\n**Fix:** Add alt text that states the insight, or bind it to a measure for dynamic text."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://learn.microsoft.com/power-bi/create-reports/desktop-accessibility-creating-reports",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "pillar": "accessibility",
                "severity": "High",
                "check": "D",
                "type": "defect",
                "tags": [
                  "power-bi",
                  "pbip",
                  "accessibility"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "A11Y-04",
              "name": "TabOrderDoesNotFollowReadingOrder",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Tab order does not follow reading order"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Keyboard users jump around the page when tab order ignores the visual layout."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "How to verify: Compare `position.tabOrder` with a top-to-bottom, left-to-right order (visuals within the row band, default 40px, share a row); flag when more than the tolerance (default 40%) of pairs are inverted. Both are configurable.\nFix: Set the tab order in the Selection pane.",
                "markdown": "**How to verify:** Compare `position.tabOrder` with a top-to-bottom, left-to-right order (visuals within the row band, default 40px, share a row); flag when more than the tolerance (default 40%) of pairs are inverted. Both are configurable.\n\n**Fix:** Set the tab order in the Selection pane."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://learn.microsoft.com/power-bi/create-reports/desktop-accessibility-creating-reports",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "pillar": "accessibility",
                "severity": "Low",
                "check": "D",
                "type": "recommendation",
                "tags": [
                  "power-bi",
                  "pbip",
                  "accessibility"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "A11Y-05",
              "name": "InsufficientTextOrGraphicsContrast",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Insufficient text or graphics contrast"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "WCAG 2.2 requires 4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text (18pt+) and 3:1 for graphical objects such as series colours."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "How to verify: The scanner resolves the base + custom theme and `ThemeDataColor` references and computes WCAG relative-luminance contrast for: theme foreground and text classes against the theme background; literal or theme font colours in visuals against the visual, page or theme background (only when every plausible background fails, and never when a shape or image sits underneath); and the first N custom-theme data colours against the background (Medium). Measure-driven colours are not assessable offline; the agent checks the remaining cases by hand.\nFix: Adjust the theme palette or the visual's font/background colours.",
                "markdown": "**How to verify:** The scanner resolves the base + custom theme and `ThemeDataColor` references and computes WCAG relative-luminance contrast for: theme foreground and text classes against the theme background; literal or theme font colours in visuals against the visual, page or theme background (only when every plausible background fails, and never when a shape or image sits underneath); and the first N custom-theme data colours against the background (Medium). Measure-driven colours are not assessable offline; the agent checks the remaining cases by hand.\n\n**Fix:** Adjust the theme palette or the visual's font/background colours."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "pillar": "accessibility",
                "severity": "High",
                "check": "D",
                "type": "defect",
                "tags": [
                  "power-bi",
                  "pbip",
                  "accessibility"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "A11Y-07",
              "name": "SeriesColoursConfusableUnderColourVisionDeficiency",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Series colours confusable under colour-vision deficiency"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "About 1 in 12 men have a red-green colour-vision deficiency. Two series colours that look distinct to most readers can collapse into one, so legends and comparisons stop working."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "How to verify: Simulate protanopia and deuteranopia (Machado et al. 2009) on the first N data colours of a custom theme and flag pairs whose CIELAB delta E falls below the threshold (default 10) while being clearly distinct (2x threshold) for normal vision.\nFix: Replace one colour of each pair (vary lightness, not only hue), or add markers, patterns or direct labels.",
                "markdown": "**How to verify:** Simulate protanopia and deuteranopia (Machado et al. 2009) on the first N data colours of a custom theme and flag pairs whose CIELAB delta E falls below the threshold (default 10) while being clearly distinct (2x threshold) for normal vision.\n\n**Fix:** Replace one colour of each pair (vary lightness, not only hue), or add markers, patterns or direct labels."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/use-of-color.html",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "pillar": "accessibility",
                "severity": "Medium",
                "check": "D",
                "type": "defect",
                "tags": [
                  "power-bi",
                  "pbip",
                  "accessibility"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "BIND-01",
              "name": "ReportFieldReferencesAModelObjectThatDoesNotExist",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Report field references a model object that does not exist"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A visual, filter or bookmark that points at a missing table, column, measure or hierarchy renders as an error (or silently drops a filter) for every viewer. No local tool checks this offline."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "How to verify: Index every `SourceRef.Entity` + `Property` in visual.json, page.json, report.json and bookmarks (resolving `Source` aliases through `From`) and look each one up in the TMDL tables, columns, measures, hierarchies and reportExtensions.json.\nFix: Rebind the field in Desktop (or edit the JSON) to the renamed object, or restore the object in the model.",
                "markdown": "**How to verify:** Index every `SourceRef.Entity` + `Property` in visual.json, page.json, report.json and bookmarks (resolving `Source` aliases through `From`) and look each one up in the TMDL tables, columns, measures, hierarchies and reportExtensions.json.\n\n**Fix:** Rebind the field in Desktop (or edit the JSON) to the renamed object, or restore the object in the model."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://learn.microsoft.com/power-bi/developer/projects/projects-report",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "pillar": "model",
                "severity": "Critical",
                "check": "D",
                "type": "defect",
                "tags": [
                  "power-bi",
                  "pbip",
                  "model"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "BIND-03",
              "name": "BookmarkStoresStateForAModelObjectThatNoLongerExists",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Bookmark stores state for a model object that no longer exists"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Bookmarks snapshot visual query state. After a measure or column is renamed or deleted, applying the bookmark can restore a broken field list."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "How to verify: Model references inside `bookmarks/*.bookmark.json` that do not resolve against the TMDL.\nFix: Re-capture (update) the bookmark after fixing the page, or delete it if unused.",
                "markdown": "**How to verify:** Model references inside `bookmarks/*.bookmark.json` that do not resolve against the TMDL.\n\n**Fix:** Re-capture (update) the bookmark after fixing the page, or delete it if unused."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://learn.microsoft.com/power-bi/create-reports/desktop-bookmarks",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "pillar": "model",
                "severity": "High",
                "check": "D",
                "type": "defect",
                "tags": [
                  "power-bi",
                  "pbip",
                  "model"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "DAX-01",
              "name": "DivisionOperatorInsteadOfDivide",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Division operator instead of DIVIDE"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "`/` raises an error or returns infinity when the denominator is zero or blank; DIVIDE handles it."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "How to verify: A `/` in a measure whose denominator is not a numeric constant (strings, comments and names are stripped first).\nFix: Use `DIVIDE(numerator, denominator)`.",
                "markdown": "**How to verify:** A `/` in a measure whose denominator is not a numeric constant (strings, comments and names are stripped first).\n\n**Fix:** Use `DIVIDE(numerator, denominator)`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://learn.microsoft.com/dax/best-practices/dax-divide-function-operator",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "pillar": "dax",
                "severity": "Medium",
                "check": "D",
                "type": "defect",
                "tags": [
                  "power-bi",
                  "pbip",
                  "dax"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "DAX-03",
              "name": "IferrorIserror",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "IFERROR / ISERROR"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Error functions force row-by-row evaluation and hide data problems."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "How to verify: `IFERROR(` or `ISERROR(` in any DAX expression.\nFix: Use DIVIDE, defensive conditions, or fix the data.",
                "markdown": "**How to verify:** `IFERROR(` or `ISERROR(` in any DAX expression.\n\n**Fix:** Use DIVIDE, defensive conditions, or fix the data."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://learn.microsoft.com/dax/best-practices/dax-error-functions",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "pillar": "dax",
                "severity": "Medium",
                "check": "D",
                "type": "defect",
                "tags": [
                  "power-bi",
                  "pbip",
                  "dax"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "DAX-04",
              "name": "BlankConvertedToZero",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "BLANK converted to zero"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Turning BLANK into 0 makes visuals show every dimension member and can slow queries; sometimes it is intended."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "How to verify: `DIVIDE(a, b, 0)`; confirm intent before raising severity.\nFix: Return BLANK, or apply the zero only in the visual (show items with no data).",
                "markdown": "**How to verify:** `DIVIDE(a, b, 0)`; confirm intent before raising severity.\n\n**Fix:** Return BLANK, or apply the zero only in the visual (show items with no data)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://learn.microsoft.com/dax/best-practices/dax-avoid-converting-blank",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "pillar": "dax",
                "severity": "Low",
                "check": "D",
                "type": "recommendation",
                "tags": [
                  "power-bi",
                  "pbip",
                  "dax"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "DAX-07",
              "name": "VisibleMeasureWithoutAFormatString",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Visible measure without a format string"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Unformatted measures show raw decimals and inconsistent units across visuals and in Copilot answers."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "How to verify: Visible measures with no `formatString` and no `formatStringDefinition`. Measures that look textual (name suggests title/label/colour, or the expression uses FORMAT, SELECTEDVALUE, CONCATENATEX, `&` or returns string literals) are skipped.\nFix: Set a format string on every visible measure.",
                "markdown": "**How to verify:** Visible measures with no `formatString` and no `formatStringDefinition`. Measures that look textual (name suggests title/label/colour, or the expression uses FORMAT, SELECTEDVALUE, CONCATENATEX, `&` or returns string literals) are skipped.\n\n**Fix:** Set a format string on every visible measure."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/TabularEditor/BestPracticeRules",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "pillar": "dax",
                "severity": "Medium",
                "check": "D",
                "type": "defect",
                "tags": [
                  "power-bi",
                  "pbip",
                  "dax"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "DAX-08",
              "name": "TodoFixmeLeftInDax",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "TODO / FIXME left in DAX"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Open work notes in production measures signal unfinished logic."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "How to verify: `TODO`, `FIXME` or `HACK` inside a DAX expression.\nFix: Resolve or move the note to the issue tracker.",
                "markdown": "**How to verify:** `TODO`, `FIXME` or `HACK` inside a DAX expression.\n\n**Fix:** Resolve or move the note to the issue tracker."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/TabularEditor/BestPracticeRules",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "pillar": "dax",
                "severity": "Low",
                "check": "D",
                "type": "defect",
                "tags": [
                  "power-bi",
                  "pbip",
                  "dax"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GOV-01",
              "name": "VisibleMeasureWithoutADescription",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Visible measure without a description"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Descriptions show in tooltips, field lists and feed Copilot/Q&A grounding. Missing descriptions are the main AI-readiness gap."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "How to verify: Visible measures without a `///` description line.\nFix: Add a one-sentence description that says what the measure counts and any window or exclusion.",
                "markdown": "**How to verify:** Visible measures without a `///` description line.\n\n**Fix:** Add a one-sentence description that says what the measure counts and any window or exclusion."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://learn.microsoft.com/power-bi/create-reports/copilot-prepare-data-ai",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "pillar": "governance",
                "severity": "Medium",
                "check": "D",
                "type": "defect",
                "tags": [
                  "power-bi",
                  "pbip",
                  "governance"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GOV-02",
              "name": "DescriptionLongerThan200Characters",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Description longer than 200 characters"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Copilot and tooltips truncate long descriptions."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "How to verify: `///` description over 200 characters on a measure, column or table.\nFix: Keep the first sentence self-contained; move detail to documentation.",
                "markdown": "**How to verify:** `///` description over 200 characters on a measure, column or table.\n\n**Fix:** Keep the first sentence self-contained; move detail to documentation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://learn.microsoft.com/power-bi/create-reports/copilot-semantic-models",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "pillar": "governance",
                "severity": "Low",
                "check": "D",
                "type": "defect",
                "tags": [
                  "power-bi",
                  "pbip",
                  "governance"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GOV-09",
              "name": "CredentialInMOrSharedExpression",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Credential in M or shared expression"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Passwords in source control leak to everyone with repository access."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "How to verify: `password=` / `pwd=` patterns in partition sources and expressions.tmdl.\nFix: Remove the secret, rotate it and use gateway / data-source credentials.",
                "markdown": "**How to verify:** `password=` / `pwd=` patterns in partition sources and expressions.tmdl.\n\n**Fix:** Remove the secret, rotate it and use gateway / data-source credentials."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://learn.microsoft.com/analysis-services/tmdl/tmdl-overview",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "pillar": "governance",
                "severity": "Critical",
                "check": "D",
                "type": "defect",
                "tags": [
                  "power-bi",
                  "pbip",
                  "governance"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GOV-14",
              "name": "PageOrVisualFolderNameIgnoredByDesktop",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Page or visual folder name ignored by Desktop"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Folder names that are not word characters or hyphens are silently ignored as private files, so the page or visual disappears."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "How to verify: Folder names under `pages/` and `visuals/` not matching `^[\\w-]+$`.\nFix: Rename the folder to letters, digits, underscores or hyphens.",
                "markdown": "**How to verify:** Folder names under `pages/` and `visuals/` not matching `^[\\w-]+$`.\n\n**Fix:** Rename the folder to letters, digits, underscores or hyphens."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://learn.microsoft.com/power-bi/developer/projects/projects-report",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "pillar": "governance",
                "severity": "High",
                "check": "D",
                "type": "defect",
                "tags": [
                  "power-bi",
                  "pbip",
                  "governance"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GOV-15",
              "name": "UnparseableJsonOrTmdl",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Unparseable JSON or TMDL"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Desktop refuses to open a project with invalid files."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "How to verify: JSON decode errors and unrecognised TMDL lines.\nFix: Fix the file (usually a merge conflict or manual edit).",
                "markdown": "**How to verify:** JSON decode errors and unrecognised TMDL lines.\n\n**Fix:** Fix the file (usually a merge conflict or manual edit)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://learn.microsoft.com/power-bi/developer/projects/projects-report",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "pillar": "governance",
                "severity": "High",
                "check": "D",
                "type": "defect",
                "tags": [
                  "power-bi",
                  "pbip",
                  "governance"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "IN-01",
              "name": "HiddenFilterCarryBusiness",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Hidden filter (may carry business logic)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Filters hidden from the filter pane change numbers without the reader knowing. Often legitimate (scope), so confirm intent."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "How to verify: `isHiddenInViewMode: true` on a report, page or visual filter.\nFix: Lock instead of hide, or state the scope in the title / description.",
                "markdown": "**How to verify:** `isHiddenInViewMode: true` on a report, page or visual filter.\n\n**Fix:** Lock instead of hide, or state the scope in the title / description."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://learn.microsoft.com/power-bi/create-reports/power-bi-report-filter",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "pillar": "interaction",
                "severity": "Medium",
                "check": "D",
                "type": "recommendation",
                "tags": [
                  "power-bi",
                  "pbip",
                  "interaction"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "IN-02",
              "name": "HiddenSlicerInASyncGroup",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Hidden slicer in a sync group"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A hidden synced slicer filters the page invisibly; the reader sees the effect but not the control."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "How to verify: Slicer with `isHidden: true` and a `syncGroup`, with no visible slicer on the same field on that page.\nFix: Show the slicer, or show the active selection in a title/card.",
                "markdown": "**How to verify:** Slicer with `isHidden: true` and a `syncGroup`, with no visible slicer on the same field on that page.\n\n**Fix:** Show the slicer, or show the active selection in a title/card."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://learn.microsoft.com/power-bi/visuals/power-bi-visualization-slicers",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "pillar": "interaction",
                "severity": "High",
                "check": "D",
                "type": "defect",
                "tags": [
                  "power-bi",
                  "pbip",
                  "interaction"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "IN-03",
              "name": "SyncGroupMixesDifferentFields",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Sync group mixes different fields"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Slicers on different fields sharing one sync group push selections onto the wrong field, silently filtering the wrong dimension."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "How to verify: `visual.syncGroup.groupName` shared by slicers bound to different fields.\nFix: Give each field its own sync group.",
                "markdown": "**How to verify:** `visual.syncGroup.groupName` shared by slicers bound to different fields.\n\n**Fix:** Give each field its own sync group."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://learn.microsoft.com/power-bi/visuals/power-bi-visualization-slicers",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "pillar": "interaction",
                "severity": "High",
                "check": "D",
                "type": "defect",
                "tags": [
                  "power-bi",
                  "pbip",
                  "interaction"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "IN-04",
              "name": "SameFieldSlicedInDifferentSyncGroups",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Same field sliced in different sync groups"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Slicers on the same field across pages that are in different sync groups keep separate selections, so pages disagree."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "How to verify: One field bound to slicers whose `syncGroup.groupName` differ.\nFix: Use one sync group per field unless independence is intended.",
                "markdown": "**How to verify:** One field bound to slicers whose `syncGroup.groupName` differ.\n\n**Fix:** Use one sync group per field unless independence is intended."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://learn.microsoft.com/power-bi/visuals/power-bi-visualization-slicers",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "pillar": "interaction",
                "severity": "Medium",
                "check": "D",
                "type": "defect",
                "tags": [
                  "power-bi",
                  "pbip",
                  "interaction"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "IN-05",
              "name": "RollingWindowMeasureShownWithoutAWindowLabel",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Rolling-window measure shown without a window label"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A measure that rebuilds its own date window from TODAY() and removes date filters ignores the date slicer. If the visual title does not say so, readers assume it follows the slicer. Heuristic."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "How to verify: Measure with TODAY/NOW plus REMOVEFILTERS/ALL on a date table (or DATESBETWEEN/DATESINPERIOD), bound in a visual whose title, display name, measure name and measure description contain no window words (last N, rolling, trailing, YTD, 12M, L3M, R12...).\nFix: Say the window in the title (\"Revenue, last 3 closed months\") or in a subtitle.",
                "markdown": "**How to verify:** Measure with TODAY/NOW plus REMOVEFILTERS/ALL on a date table (or DATESBETWEEN/DATESINPERIOD), bound in a visual whose title, display name, measure name and measure description contain no window words (last N, rolling, trailing, YTD, 12M, L3M, R12...).\n\n**Fix:** Say the window in the title (\"Revenue, last 3 closed months\") or in a subtitle."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://learn.microsoft.com/power-bi/guidance/model-date-tables",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
